{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019bbn2QXZPpCbdWGZBFipwR","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tnarrative_guidance: 'Composability claim becomes regime-dependent: OntoCoDec composes\n2\t  at zero cost on SciERC FT (7 relations, low tightness diversity), but DocRED FT\n3\t  (96 relations) reveals systematic constraint-model conflict. FT narrows output distribution\n4\t  (entropy ~0.7) while semantic masks enforce per-relation type rules → frequent top-token\n5\t  elimination → cascading quality loss. CF spikes because FT learns globally consistent\n6\t  entity typing that per-relation enforcement disrupts. Paper reframe: §5 adds \"regime-dependent\n7\t  cost-benefit analysis\" — OntoCoDec is most valuable in zero-shot/few-shot where\n8\t  violations are high and model calibration is poor; as FT improves model calibration,\n9\t  constraint overhead shifts from beneficial to detrimental on complex ontologies.\n10\t  Core zero-shot contribution (§4) unchanged. Target venue unchanged (EMNLP) but position\n11\t  as method + regime analysis paper.\n12\t\n13\t  '\n14\timagined_experiments:\n15\t- name: Qwen DocRED LoRA + Full S1 Constrained Eval\n16\t  plan_id: w5_qwen_docred_lora_constrained_eval\n17\t  description: 'Evaluate Qwen3-8B LoRA-finetuned on DocRED with full_s1 (grammar+semantic)\n18\t    constrained decoding. Tests whether OntoCoDec composes with FT on a 96-relation\n19\t    ontology. Baseline: FT unconstrained DR=0.76%, R-F1=40.86%, E-F1=82.15%, parse_fail=7.11%,\n20\t    CF=0.12%.\n21\t\n22\t    '\n23\t  expected_results:\n24\t    DR_pct: 0.25\n25\t    RV_pct: 0.0\n26\t    ET_pct: 0.0\n27\t    CF_pct: 5.8\n28\t    R_F1: 39.2\n29\t    R_precision: 36.0\n30\t    R_recall: 43.0\n31\t    E_F1: 80.3\n32\t    E_precision: 84.5\n33\t    E_recall: 76.5\n34\t    R_F1_delta_pp: -1.66\n35\t    E_F1_delta_pp: -1.85\n36\t    parse_fail_rate_pct: 12.0\n37\t    parse_fail_increase_pp: 4.9\n38\t    total_entities_pred: 17800\n39\t    total_relations_pred: 15200\n40\t    success_samples: 878\n41\t    fail_samples: 120\n42\t  result_rationale: 'DR 降至 0.25%（constraint 机制仍物理上阻止无效 domain-range 组合，不受 FT 影响），\n43\t    但代价极高。三个降质机制并行作用：\n44\t\n45\t    (1) R-F1 下降 1.66pp：Qwen DocRED FT 的训练 entropy=0.715（registry 记录）， 说明模型学到了窄而尖的\n46\t    output distribution。semantic mask 在 relation type token 位置频繁排除模型的 top-1/top-2\n47\t    候选 → 迫使生成走低概率路径 → 后续 token 基于 非预期 prefix 生成 → cascade degradation。96 个 relation\n48\t    type 意味着远多于 SciERC 的 conflict point（SciERC 7 relations，FT+constrained delta 仅\n49\t    -0.09pp）。 DocRED 中高 tightness relation（如 P31_instance_of τ≈0.95、P17_country τ≈0.90）\n50\t    的 semantic mask 最具限制性，恰好也是 FT 模型置信度最高的 relation → conflict 最严重。\n51\t\n52\t    (2) CF 从 0.12% 飙升至 5.8%：FT 模型学到了全局一致的 entity typing（训练数据中 同一 entity 在不同 relation\n53\t    中 type 一致），但 semantic 层逐 relation 独立 enforce type constraint。FT 的 strong prior\n54\t    与 per-relation enforcement 冲突 → 同一 entity 在不同 relation triple 中被 semantic mask\n55\t    强制赋予不同 type（EVR drift）。 zero-shot Qwen DocRED CF 仅 2.57%，FT 使模型 prior 更强 → conflict\n56\t    更系统化 → CF 翻倍。但低于 Llama 预期值，因为 Qwen FT parse_fail=7.11% 过滤掉了部分冲突严重的样本。\n57\t\n58\t    (3) parse_fail 从 7.11% 增至 12.0%（+4.9pp）：FT 的窄 distribution + semantic mask 的 token\n59\t    排除 → 更频繁出现 grammar ∩ semantic = ∅ 的 empty intersection。fallback 到 grammar-only\n60\t    后，部分 doc 的 JSON 结构在 constraint recovery 过程中损坏 → parse failure。Qwen 本身在 DocRED\n61\t    上 parse_fail baseline 已偏高（unconstrained 7.11% vs Llama 2.3%），constraint 叠加后进一步恶化。\n62\t\n63\t    E-F1 下降 1.85pp 的机制：semantic mask 在 entity type token 位置强制修改 FT 学到的 type assignment\n64\t    → entity list 中的 type 被改动 → all_set 评估下 type 变动导致 部分 entity match 失败 → recall\n65\t    从 79.11% 降至 76.5%。precision 仅小幅下降因为 grammar 仍消除 OOV entity type（ET→0%）。\n66\t\n67\t    '\n68\t  tables:\n69\t  - name: 'Table: Qwen DocRED FT Composability (2×2)'\n70\t    columns:\n71\t    - Config\n72\t    - DR_pct\n73\t    - CF_pct\n74\t    - R_F1\n75\t    - E_F1\n76\t    - parse_fail_pct\n77\t    rows:\n78\t    - - FT unconstrained\n79\t      - 0.76\n80\t      - 0.12\n81\t      - 40.86\n82\t      - 82.15\n83\t      - 7.11\n84\t    - - FT constrained (worst)\n85\t      - 0.25\n86\t      - 5.8\n87\t      - 39.2\n88\t      - 80.3\n89\t      - 12.0\n90\t    - - ZS unconstrained\n91\t      - 18.46\n92\t      - 0.1\n93\t      - 7.74\n94\t      - 58.15\n95\t      - 1.2\n96\t    - - ZS constrained\n97\t      - 10.21\n98\t      - 2.57\n99\t      - 8.23\n100\t      - 59.37\n101\t      - 1.1\n102\t  figures_description:\n103\t  - 'Bar chart: R-F1 delta (constrained−unconstrained) for Qwen across 4 regimes:\n104\t    ZS-SciERC (+0.13pp), ZS-DocRED (+0.50pp), FT-SciERC (-0.09pp), FT-DocRED (-1.66pp).\n105\t    Shows clear regime dependence — positive in ZS, negative in FT-DocRED.'\n106\t  - 'Scatter: CF rate (y) vs constraint tightness τ̄ (x) across {ZS, FT} × {SciERC,\n107\t    DocRED}. FT-DocRED is the outlier in the upper-right quadrant.'\n108\t  analysis: 'Qwen DocRED 的 worst-tier 核心发现：constraint 仍消除 DR（0.76%→0.25%，↓67%）， 但\n109\t    R-F1 代价 1.66pp 在 FT regime 下不可接受——FT unconstrained 本身 DR 已很低（0.76%）， 为消除 0.51pp\n110\t    残余 DR 付出 1.66pp R-F1 是 3.3:1 的不利交换比。 对比 zero-shot：DR 18.46%→10.21%（↓44.7%）同时 R-F1\n111\t    +0.50pp，这是 win-win。 结论：OntoCoDec 的 ROI 在 FT regime 下急剧下降。parse_fail 增至 12% 进一步削弱\n112\t    practical value。论文 framing 必须明确标注\"FT+complex ontology\"为 unfavorable regime。\n113\t\n114\t    '\n115\t- name: Llama DocRED LoRA + Full S1 Constrained Eval\n116\t  plan_id: w5_llama_docred_lora_constrained_eval\n117\t  description: 'Evaluate Llama-3.1-8B LoRA-finetuned on DocRED with full_s1 (grammar+semantic)\n118\t    constrained decoding. Baseline: FT unconstrained DR=0.49%, R-F1=43.72%, E-F1=83.93%,\n119\t    parse_fail=2.3%. Llama zero-shot DocRED constrained CF already highest at 12.02%\n120\t    — FT may amplify or partially mitigate depending on whether FT-learned patterns\n121\t    align with ontology constraints.\n122\t\n123\t    '\n124\t  expected_results:\n125\t    DR_pct: 0.12\n126\t    RV_pct: 0.0\n127\t    ET_pct: 0.0\n128\t    CF_pct: 8.5\n129\t    R_F1: 42.4\n130\t    R_precision: 37.8\n131\t    R_recall: 48.5\n132\t    E_F1: 82.1\n133\t    E_precision: 84.0\n134\t    E_recall: 80.3\n135\t    R_F1_delta_pp: -1.32\n136\t    E_F1_delta_pp: -1.83\n137\t    parse_fail_rate_pct: 7.0\n138\t    parse_fail_increase_pp: 4.7\n139\t    total_entities_pred: 18700\n140\t    total_relations_pred: 15800\n141\t    documents_checked: 928\n142\t    parse_failures: 70\n143\t  result_rationale: 'DR 降至 0.12%（Llama FT unconstrained DR=0.49% 本就极低，constraint 几乎完全消除\n144\t    残余），但 three-way degradation 与 Qwen 平行：\n145\t\n146\t    (1) R-F1 下降 1.32pp：Llama FT 的 R-F1=43.72% 高于 Qwen（40.86%），说明 Llama FT 学到了更优的 extraction\n147\t    pattern。但这也意味着 constraint 干预对 Llama 造成的 绝对质量损失更 meaningful。机制同 Qwen：semantic mask\n148\t    排除 FT top-token → 低概率 path → cascade。delta 略小于 Qwen（-1.32 vs -1.66）的原因：Llama FT\n149\t    unconstrained RV=0.15%（vs Qwen 0.27%），说明 Llama FT 生成的 relation name 更规范 → grammar\n150\t    层 干预更少 → cascade 起点更少。但仍在 worst tier 范围 [-2.0, -0.8] 内。\n151\t\n152\t    (2) CF 从 ~0% 飙升至 8.5%：这是 worst tier 的核心 signal。Llama zero-shot DocRED constrained\n153\t    CF=12.02%（registry 实测），说明 Llama 的 entity typing prior 与 DocRED ontology 的 per-relation\n154\t    type constraint 存在系统性 mismatch。FT 后 CF 降至 8.5% 而非继续上升，因为 FT 数据中包含 ontology-consistent\n155\t    的 type assignment，部分 校正了 zero-shot 的 mismatch。但 8.5% 仍远高于 unconstrained（~0%）：FT\n156\t    学到的 全局一致 typing 与 semantic 层的 per-relation enforcement 仍存在不可调和的冲突。 Llama CF >\n157\t    Qwen CF（8.5 vs 5.8）的原因：Llama 在 DocRED 上的 entity typing 更 decisive（probability\n158\t    mass 更集中），semantic mask override 时产生的 drift 更大。\n159\t\n160\t    (3) parse_fail 从 2.3% 增至 7.0%（+4.7pp）：Llama FT baseline parse_fail=2.3% 远 低于 Qwen（7.11%），说明\n161\t    Llama FT 的 JSON 结构生成更稳定。但 constraint 叠加后 增幅与 Qwen 相当（+4.7 vs +4.9pp），证明 parse\n162\t    failure 增量主要由 constraint mechanism 驱动而非模型固有能力。empty intersection fallback → grammar-only\n163\t    recovery → 部分样本的 JSON 嵌套结构在 recovery 中断裂 → parse failure。\n164\t\n165\t    E-F1 下降 1.83pp（83.93→82.1）：Llama zero-shot constrained E-F1 也下降了 0.64pp （55.65→55.01），FT\n166\t    下降幅度更大因为 FT 的 entity typing 更精确、被 override 时 损失更大。Llama 的 entity typing 在 FT 后达到\n167\t    E-F1=83.93%（高于 Qwen 82.15%）， constraint 对高质量 typing 的干扰造成的绝对损失更大。\n168\t\n169\t    '\n170\t  tables:\n171\t  - name: 'Table: Llama DocRED FT Composability (2×2)'\n172\t    columns:\n173\t    - Config\n174\t    - DR_pct\n175\t    - CF_pct\n176\t    - R_F1\n177\t    - E_F1\n178\t    - parse_fail_pct\n179\t    rows:\n180\t    - - FT unconstrained\n181\t      - 0.49\n182\t      - 0.0\n183\t      - 43.72\n184\t      - 83.93\n185\t      - 2.3\n186\t    - - FT constrained (worst)\n187\t      - 0.12\n188\t      - 8.5\n189\t      - 42.4\n190\t      - 82.1\n191\t      - 7.0\n192\t    - - ZS unconstrained\n193\t      - 26.07\n194\t      - 0.17\n195\t      - 5.98\n196\t      - 55.65\n197\t      - 6.8\n198\t    - - ZS constrained\n199\t      - 2.55\n200\t      - 12.02\n201\t      - 6.27\n202\t      - 55.01\n203\t      - 9.1\n204\t  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model FT Composability Summary (DocRED)'\n205\t    columns:\n206\t    - Metric\n207\t    - Qwen_delta\n208\t    - Llama_delta\n209\t    - Interpretation\n210\t    rows:\n211\t    - - R-F1 delta (pp)\n212\t      - -1.66\n213\t      - -1.32\n214\t      - Both models show significant degradation\n215\t    - - E-F1 delta (pp)\n216\t      - -1.85\n217\t      - -1.83\n218\t      - Comparable entity quality loss\n219\t    - - CF increase (pp)\n220\t      - 5.68\n221\t      - 8.5\n222\t      - Llama more CF-sensitive (consistent with ZS pattern)\n223\t    - - DR residual (%)\n224\t      - 0.25\n225\t      - 0.12\n226\t      - Constraint mechanism still works\n227\t    - - parse_fail increase (pp)\n228\t      - 4.9\n229\t      - 4.7\n230\t      - Similar mechanism-driven increase\n231\t  figures_description:\n232\t  - 'Grouped bar chart: R-F1 delta across all 8 conditions {Qwen,Llama} × {SciERC,DocRED}\n233\t    × {ZS,FT}. ZS deltas cluster near 0/positive; FT-DocRED deltas are both negative.\n234\t    Visual thesis: composability cost is regime × ontology-complexity dependent.'\n235\t  - 'Line plot: CF rate trajectory across 4 configs (ZS-uncon → ZS-con → FT-uncon\n236\t    → FT-con) for both models. Llama line spikes at ZS-con then partially recovers\n237\t    at FT-con; Qwen line rises monotonically. Shows FT partially corrects ZS typing\n238\t    mismatch but introduces new FT-specific conflicts.'\n239\t  - 'Heatmap: 2×2 matrix (model × regime) with cell color = ''net value score'' defined\n240\t    as DR_reduction_pp − R_F1_loss_pp. Green cells (ZS) = positive net value; red\n241\t    cells (FT-DocRED) = negative net value. One-glance summary of when OntoCoDec helps\n242\t    vs hurts.'\n243\t  analysis: \"Llama DocRED 的 worst-tier 结果与 Qwen 形成一致 pattern：constraint 仍消除 DR （0.49%→0.12%，↓76%），但\\\n244\t    \\ R-F1 代价 1.32pp 同样不利。交换比：消除 0.37pp DR 付出 1.32pp R-F1 = 3.6:1 不利。CF=8.5% 虽低于 zero-shot（12.02%），但仍是\\\n245\t    \\ unconstrained 的 ∞ 倍（0→8.5%）。\\n跨模型一致性：两个模型在 FT-DocRED 上均展现 {DR↓, R-F1↓, CF↑,\\\n246\t    \\ parse_fail↑} 的一致 pattern，且 delta 量级相当。这排除了\\\"单一模型 artifact\\\"的可能 —— 是 constraint-FT\\\n247\t    \\ interaction 的系统性效应。\\nSciERC vs DocRED 对比：SciERC FT+constrained 几乎零成本（两个模型 delta\\\n248\t    \\ < 0.1pp）， DocRED 显著负面。决定性差异：ontology complexity（7 vs 96 relations）和 average\\\n249\t    \\ tightness（SciERC τ̄≈0.65 vs DocRED τ̄≈0.84）。更多 relation + 更高 tightness = 更多\\\n250\t    \\ constraint-model conflict point = 更大 cascade degradation。\\n论文 §5 讨论建议的结构： (1)\\\n251\t    \\ 定义 \\\"constraint ROI\\\" = DR_reduction_pp / R_F1_cost_pp (2) ZS regime：ROI >>\\\n252\t    \\ 1（SciERC: ∞, DocRED: positive with F1 gain） (3) FT regime + simple ontology：ROI\\\n253\t    \\ ≈ ∞（SciERC FT: zero cost） (4) FT regime + complex ontology：ROI < 1（DocRED FT:\\\n254\t    \\ 3-4x unfavorable） (5) Recommendation：OntoCoDec for deployment without FT data\\\n255\t    \\ or with simple ontology;\\n    skip constraint decoding when FT + complex ontology（model\\\n256\t    \\ self-calibration suffices）\"\n257\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8f7b9b0-e3ba-485f-a37e-4e472b218b82","uuid":"f1a560b9-e026-4643-96d4-84fb142b8409","timestamp":"2026-05-16T02:51:21.652Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_6/projects/schema_semantic_constrained_ie/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260516T021434/worst/review_context.yaml","content":"narrative_guidance: 'Composability claim becomes regime-dependent: OntoCoDec composes\n  at zero cost on SciERC FT (7 relations, low tightness diversity), but DocRED FT\n  (96 relations) reveals systematic constraint-model conflict. FT narrows output distribution\n  (entropy ~0.7) while semantic masks enforce per-relation type rules → frequent top-token\n  elimination → cascading quality loss. CF spikes because FT learns globally consistent\n  entity typing that per-relation enforcement disrupts. Paper reframe: §5 adds \"regime-dependent\n  cost-benefit analysis\" — OntoCoDec is most valuable in zero-shot/few-shot where\n  violations are high and model calibration is poor; as FT improves model calibration,\n  constraint overhead shifts from beneficial to detrimental on complex ontologies.\n  Core zero-shot contribution (§4) unchanged. Target venue unchanged (EMNLP) but position\n  as method + regime analysis paper.\n\n  '\nimagined_experiments:\n- name: Qwen DocRED LoRA + Full S1 Constrained Eval\n  plan_id: w5_qwen_docred_lora_constrained_eval\n  description: 'Evaluate Qwen3-8B LoRA-finetuned on DocRED with full_s1 (grammar+semantic)\n    constrained decoding. Tests whether OntoCoDec composes with FT on a 96-relation\n    ontology. Baseline: FT unconstrained DR=0.76%, R-F1=40.86%, E-F1=82.15%, parse_fail=7.11%,\n    CF=0.12%.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    DR_pct: 0.25\n    RV_pct: 0.0\n    ET_pct: 0.0\n    CF_pct: 5.8\n    R_F1: 39.2\n    R_precision: 36.0\n    R_recall: 43.0\n    E_F1: 80.3\n    E_precision: 84.5\n    E_recall: 76.5\n    R_F1_delta_pp: -1.66\n    E_F1_delta_pp: -1.85\n    parse_fail_rate_pct: 12.0\n    parse_fail_increase_pp: 4.9\n    total_entities_pred: 17800\n    total_relations_pred: 15200\n    success_samples: 878\n    fail_samples: 120\n  result_rationale: 'DR 降至 0.25%（constraint 机制仍物理上阻止无效 domain-range 组合，不受 FT 影响），\n    但代价极高。三个降质机制并行作用：\n\n    (1) R-F1 下降 1.66pp：Qwen DocRED FT 的训练 entropy=0.715（registry 记录）， 说明模型学到了窄而尖的\n    output distribution。semantic mask 在 relation type token 位置频繁排除模型的 top-1/top-2\n    候选 → 迫使生成走低概率路径 → 后续 token 基于 非预期 prefix 生成 → cascade degradation。96 个 relation\n    type 意味着远多于 SciERC 的 conflict point（SciERC 7 relations，FT+constrained delta 仅\n    -0.09pp）。 DocRED 中高 tightness relation（如 P31_instance_of τ≈0.95、P17_country τ≈0.90）\n    的 semantic mask 最具限制性，恰好也是 FT 模型置信度最高的 relation → conflict 最严重。\n\n    (2) CF 从 0.12% 飙升至 5.8%：FT 模型学到了全局一致的 entity typing（训练数据中 同一 entity 在不同 relation\n    中 type 一致），但 semantic 层逐 relation 独立 enforce type constraint。FT 的 strong prior\n    与 per-relation enforcement 冲突 → 同一 entity 在不同 relation triple 中被 semantic mask\n    强制赋予不同 type（EVR drift）。 zero-shot Qwen DocRED CF 仅 2.57%，FT 使模型 prior 更强 → conflict\n    更系统化 → CF 翻倍。但低于 Llama 预期值，因为 Qwen FT parse_fail=7.11% 过滤掉了部分冲突严重的样本。\n\n    (3) parse_fail 从 7.11% 增至 12.0%（+4.9pp）：FT 的窄 distribution + semantic mask 的 token\n    排除 → 更频繁出现 grammar ∩ semantic = ∅ 的 empty intersection。fallback 到 grammar-only\n    后，部分 doc 的 JSON 结构在 constraint recovery 过程中损坏 → parse failure。Qwen 本身在 DocRED\n    上 parse_fail baseline 已偏高（unconstrained 7.11% vs Llama 2.3%），constraint 叠加后进一步恶化。\n\n    E-F1 下降 1.85pp 的机制：semantic mask 在 entity type token 位置强制修改 FT 学到的 type assignment\n    → entity list 中的 type 被改动 → all_set 评估下 type 变动导致 部分 entity match 失败 → recall\n    从 79.11% 降至 76.5%。precision 仅小幅下降因为 grammar 仍消除 OOV entity type（ET→0%）。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Qwen DocRED FT Composability (2×2)'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - DR_pct\n    - CF_pct\n    - R_F1\n    - E_F1\n    - parse_fail_pct\n    rows:\n    - - FT unconstrained\n      - 0.76\n      - 0.12\n      - 40.86\n      - 82.15\n      - 7.11\n    - - FT constrained (worst)\n      - 0.25\n      - 5.8\n      - 39.2\n      - 80.3\n      - 12.0\n    - - ZS unconstrained\n      - 18.46\n      - 0.1\n      - 7.74\n      - 58.15\n      - 1.2\n    - - ZS constrained\n      - 10.21\n      - 2.57\n      - 8.23\n      - 59.37\n      - 1.1\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Bar chart: R-F1 delta (constrained−unconstrained) for Qwen across 4 regimes:\n    ZS-SciERC (+0.13pp), ZS-DocRED (+0.50pp), FT-SciERC (-0.09pp), FT-DocRED (-1.66pp).\n    Shows clear regime dependence — positive in ZS, negative in FT-DocRED.'\n  - 'Scatter: CF rate (y) vs constraint tightness τ̄ (x) across {ZS, FT} × {SciERC,\n    DocRED}. FT-DocRED is the outlier in the upper-right quadrant.'\n  analysis: 'Qwen DocRED 的 worst-tier 核心发现：constraint 仍消除 DR（0.76%→0.25%，↓67%）， 但\n    R-F1 代价 1.66pp 在 FT regime 下不可接受——FT unconstrained 本身 DR 已很低（0.76%）， 为消除 0.51pp\n    残余 DR 付出 1.66pp R-F1 是 3.3:1 的不利交换比。 对比 zero-shot：DR 18.46%→10.21%（↓44.7%）同时 R-F1\n    +0.50pp，这是 win-win。 结论：OntoCoDec 的 ROI 在 FT regime 下急剧下降。parse_fail 增至 12% 进一步削弱\n    practical value。论文 framing 必须明确标注\"FT+complex ontology\"为 unfavorable regime。\n\n    '\n- name: Llama DocRED LoRA + Full S1 Constrained Eval\n  plan_id: w5_llama_docred_lora_constrained_eval\n  description: 'Evaluate Llama-3.1-8B LoRA-finetuned on DocRED with full_s1 (grammar+semantic)\n    constrained decoding. Baseline: FT unconstrained DR=0.49%, R-F1=43.72%, E-F1=83.93%,\n    parse_fail=2.3%. Llama zero-shot DocRED constrained CF already highest at 12.02%\n    — FT may amplify or partially mitigate depending on whether FT-learned patterns\n    align with ontology constraints.\n\n    '\n  expected_results:\n    DR_pct: 0.12\n    RV_pct: 0.0\n    ET_pct: 0.0\n    CF_pct: 8.5\n    R_F1: 42.4\n    R_precision: 37.8\n    R_recall: 48.5\n    E_F1: 82.1\n    E_precision: 84.0\n    E_recall: 80.3\n    R_F1_delta_pp: -1.32\n    E_F1_delta_pp: -1.83\n    parse_fail_rate_pct: 7.0\n    parse_fail_increase_pp: 4.7\n    total_entities_pred: 18700\n    total_relations_pred: 15800\n    documents_checked: 928\n    parse_failures: 70\n  result_rationale: 'DR 降至 0.12%（Llama FT unconstrained DR=0.49% 本就极低，constraint 几乎完全消除\n    残余），但 three-way degradation 与 Qwen 平行：\n\n    (1) R-F1 下降 1.32pp：Llama FT 的 R-F1=43.72% 高于 Qwen（40.86%），说明 Llama FT 学到了更优的 extraction\n    pattern。但这也意味着 constraint 干预对 Llama 造成的 绝对质量损失更 meaningful。机制同 Qwen：semantic mask\n    排除 FT top-token → 低概率 path → cascade。delta 略小于 Qwen（-1.32 vs -1.66）的原因：Llama FT\n    unconstrained RV=0.15%（vs Qwen 0.27%），说明 Llama FT 生成的 relation name 更规范 → grammar\n    层 干预更少 → cascade 起点更少。但仍在 worst tier 范围 [-2.0, -0.8] 内。\n\n    (2) CF 从 ~0% 飙升至 8.5%：这是 worst tier 的核心 signal。Llama zero-shot DocRED constrained\n    CF=12.02%（registry 实测），说明 Llama 的 entity typing prior 与 DocRED ontology 的 per-relation\n    type constraint 存在系统性 mismatch。FT 后 CF 降至 8.5% 而非继续上升，因为 FT 数据中包含 ontology-consistent\n    的 type assignment，部分 校正了 zero-shot 的 mismatch。但 8.5% 仍远高于 unconstrained（~0%）：FT\n    学到的 全局一致 typing 与 semantic 层的 per-relation enforcement 仍存在不可调和的冲突。 Llama CF >\n    Qwen CF（8.5 vs 5.8）的原因：Llama 在 DocRED 上的 entity typing 更 decisive（probability\n    mass 更集中），semantic mask override 时产生的 drift 更大。\n\n    (3) parse_fail 从 2.3% 增至 7.0%（+4.7pp）：Llama FT baseline parse_fail=2.3% 远 低于 Qwen（7.11%），说明\n    Llama FT 的 JSON 结构生成更稳定。但 constraint 叠加后 增幅与 Qwen 相当（+4.7 vs +4.9pp），证明 parse\n    failure 增量主要由 constraint mechanism 驱动而非模型固有能力。empty intersection fallback → grammar-only\n    recovery → 部分样本的 JSON 嵌套结构在 recovery 中断裂 → parse failure。\n\n    E-F1 下降 1.83pp（83.93→82.1）：Llama zero-shot constrained E-F1 也下降了 0.64pp （55.65→55.01），FT\n    下降幅度更大因为 FT 的 entity typing 更精确、被 override 时 损失更大。Llama 的 entity typing 在 FT 后达到\n    E-F1=83.93%（高于 Qwen 82.15%）， constraint 对高质量 typing 的干扰造成的绝对损失更大。\n\n    '\n  tables:\n  - name: 'Table: Llama DocRED FT Composability (2×2)'\n    columns:\n    - Config\n    - DR_pct\n    - CF_pct\n    - R_F1\n    - E_F1\n    - parse_fail_pct\n    rows:\n    - - FT unconstrained\n      - 0.49\n      - 0.0\n      - 43.72\n      - 83.93\n      - 2.3\n    - - FT constrained (worst)\n      - 0.12\n      - 8.5\n      - 42.4\n      - 82.1\n      - 7.0\n    - - ZS unconstrained\n      - 26.07\n      - 0.17\n      - 5.98\n      - 55.65\n      - 6.8\n    - - ZS constrained\n      - 2.55\n      - 12.02\n      - 6.27\n      - 55.01\n      - 9.1\n  - name: 'Table: Cross-Model FT Composability Summary (DocRED)'\n    columns:\n    - Metric\n    - Qwen_delta\n    - Llama_delta\n    - Interpretation\n    rows:\n    - - R-F1 delta (pp)\n      - -1.66\n      - -1.32\n      - Both models show significant degradation\n    - - E-F1 delta (pp)\n      - -1.85\n      - -1.83\n      - Comparable entity quality loss\n    - - CF increase (pp)\n      - 5.68\n      - 8.5\n      - Llama more CF-sensitive (consistent with ZS pattern)\n    - - DR residual (%)\n      - 0.25\n      - 0.12\n      - Constraint mechanism still works\n    - - parse_fail increase (pp)\n      - 4.9\n      - 4.7\n      - Similar mechanism-driven increase\n  figures_description:\n  - 'Grouped bar chart: R-F1 delta across all 8 conditions {Qwen,Llama} × {SciERC,DocRED}\n    × {ZS,FT}. ZS deltas cluster near 0/positive; FT-DocRED deltas are both negative.\n    Visual thesis: composability cost is regime × ontology-complexity dependent.'\n  - 'Line plot: CF rate trajectory across 4 configs (ZS-uncon → ZS-con → FT-uncon\n    → FT-con) for both models. Llama line spikes at ZS-con then partially recovers\n    at FT-con; Qwen line rises monotonically. Shows FT partially corrects ZS typing\n    mismatch but introduces new FT-specific conflicts.'\n  - 'Heatmap: 2×2 matrix (model × regime) with cell color = ''net value score'' defined\n    as DR_reduction_pp − R_F1_loss_pp. Green cells (ZS) = positive net value; red\n    cells (FT-DocRED) = negative net value. One-glance summary of when OntoCoDec helps\n    vs hurts.'\n  analysis: \"Llama DocRED 的 worst-tier 结果与 Qwen 形成一致 pattern：constraint 仍消除 DR （0.49%→0.12%，↓76%），但\\\n    \\ R-F1 代价 1.32pp 同样不利。交换比：消除 0.37pp DR 付出 1.32pp R-F1 = 3.6:1 不利。CF=8.5% 虽低于 zero-shot（12.02%），但仍是\\\n    \\ unconstrained 的 ∞ 倍（0→8.5%）。\\n跨模型一致性：两个模型在 FT-DocRED 上均展现 {DR↓, R-F1↓, CF↑,\\\n    \\ parse_fail↑} 的一致 pattern，且 delta 量级相当。这排除了\\\"单一模型 artifact\\\"的可能 —— 是 constraint-FT\\\n    \\ interaction 的系统性效应。\\nSciERC vs DocRED 对比：SciERC FT+constrained 几乎零成本（两个模型 delta\\\n    \\ < 0.1pp）， DocRED 显著负面。决定性差异：ontology complexity（7 vs 96 relations）和 average\\\n    \\ tightness（SciERC τ̄≈0.65 vs DocRED τ̄≈0.84）。更多 relation + 更高 tightness = 更多\\\n    \\ constraint-model conflict point = 更大 cascade degradation。\\n论文 §5 讨论建议的结构： (1)\\\n    \\ 定义 \\\"constraint ROI\\\" = DR_reduction_pp / R_F1_cost_pp (2) ZS regime：ROI >>\\\n    \\ 1（SciERC: ∞, DocRED: positive with F1 gain） (3) FT regime + simple ontology：ROI\\\n    \\ ≈ ∞（SciERC FT: zero cost） (4) FT regime + complex ontology：ROI < 1（DocRED FT:\\\n    \\ 3-4x unfavorable） (5) Recommendation：OntoCoDec for deployment without FT data\\\n    \\ or with simple ontology;\\n    skip constraint decoding when FT + complex ontology（model\\\n    \\ self-calibration suffices）\"\n","numLines":257,"startLine":1,"totalLines":257}}}
