{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VgpaFpkejsxcC9wYa6KXEe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Review report submitted successfully.\n\n**Consensus: 3/6 (Weak Reject)**, confidence 4/5.\n\nKey findings from the two-reviewer roundtable:\n\n1. **Results appear simulated** — reported FT+constrained numbers match the `imagined_experiments` YAML to the decimal, casting doubt on whether real experiments were conducted.\n2. **Limited technical novelty** — the grammar layer is a direct XGrammar application; the semantic layer is a straightforward hash-map + logit masking. Below the top-venue technical bar.\n3. **Overclaimed priority** — \"first to compile ontology constraints into decoding masks\" needs qualification given SynCode (ICML 2024), IterGen (ICLR 2025), and GCD (EMNLP 2023).\n4. **Insufficient experimental coverage** — no FT ablations (grammar-only, semantic-only, post-hoc filtering), no variance reporting, no latency measurements, SciERC FT not tabled.\n\n**Main strength:** The regime-dependent composability finding is genuinely useful — the paper honestly shows that constraints help in ZS but hurt in FT+complex ontology, with consistent cross-model evidence and an actionable practitioner framework. A revised version with real results, ablations, and more careful positioning could merit acceptance."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5553,"cache_read_input_tokens":56081,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5553},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8f7b9b0-e3ba-485f-a37e-4e472b218b82","uuid":"bf14f3f8-f5f7-46ec-9762-d9453e5220f3"}
